{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-51572365-8b5e-4521-afca-56d32eb12440","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb67278b91f023ce","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-jzszt08x/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Per-project idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a per-project idle and stale resource report view in the\nRHOAI web console, giving cluster administrators visibility into resources\nthat are sitting idle: workbenches nobody has touched in weeks that keep\ntheir volumes and reservations, and old pipeline runs that accumulate stored\nartifacts. The report surfaces, per project, an idle-workbench section\n(last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from the notebook\ncontroller's activity tracking, and a stale pipeline-run section (completed\nruns older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from\nKubeflow Pipelines run metadata. Both report sections are exportable as CSV\nso administrators can reclaim capacity with confidence.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a per-project report surface in the web console that shows idle and stale resources.\n- Idle-workbench report section: per workbench, show last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking), owner, and reserved resources (volumes and reservations).\n- Stale pipeline-run report section: list completed pipeline runs older than a configurable age threshold that retain artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Make the stale-run age threshold configurable.\n- CSV export of either report (idle-workbench report and stale pipeline-run report).\n- Validate that the report data correctly reflects the two passive data sources: the notebook controller's last-activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run completion metadata (no code changes to those components are in scope).\n- No automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and no cost/chargeback calculations (out of scope per strategy).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project with workbenches of varying activity, when an administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then each workbench is listed with its last activity, owner, and reserved resources, and the last-activity values match the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n- Given a project with completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run report, then runs completed before the configured age threshold are listed with their retained artifacts, and the listing matches Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Given the configurable age threshold, when an administrator changes it, then the stale pipeline-run report reflects the new threshold.\n- Given either report, when an administrator triggers CSV export, then a CSV file is produced containing the report's rows and columns.\n- Given the report view, when an administrator reviews it, then it contains no reclamation or deletion actions (out of scope).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled because it operates on the same report surfaces and data built for HLR-1/HLR-2.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28524,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83ab9b1484cafa91","agent_id":"ab937682b8c4c817c","session_id":"912108fb-652c-486d-bf9a-f0099a27506b","uuid":"19793a26-ca3c-45cf-a8e0-908e43a60f29","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:46:14.057Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","ta