{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99a6572f3772e3ff","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E002\n3\ttitle: Document the idle/stale resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 0\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 3\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Document the idle/stale resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers Red Hat documentation explaining the new per-project\n35\tidle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console: what each report\n36\tshows (idle workbenches with last activity, owner, and reserved resources;\n37\tstale pipeline runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts),\n38\thow to export them as CSV, and the safe manual steps an administrator can\n39\ttake to reclaim capacity based on the reports.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- A documentation topic introducing the idle and stale resource reports and the administrator problem they solve (reclaiming capacity with confidence).\n44\t- Guidance on reading each report section: idle-workbench entries (last activity, owner, reserved resources) and stale pipeline-run entries (completed runs older than the configurable age with retained artifacts).\n45\t- Instructions for configuring the stale-run age threshold.\n46\t- Instructions for exporting either report as CSV.\n47\t- Documented safe reclamation steps for idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs, including appropriate cautions (the platform performs no automated reclamation or deletion).\n48\t- Content outline:\n49\t  1. Overview: why idle/stale resource reporting exists\n50\t  2. Viewing the idle-workbench report\n51\t  3. Viewing the stale pipeline-run report and configuring the age threshold\n52\t  4. Exporting reports as CSV\n53\t  5. Safe reclamation steps and cautions\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Published documentation topics exist that explain both reports, the configurable age threshold, CSV export, and safe reclamation steps.\n58\t- Documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reports and accurately reflects the shipped behavior (fields shown, threshold configuration, export output).\n59\t- Reclamation guidance is reviewed for safety and clearly states that reclamation is manual (no automated deletion).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf92a77323365c5a","agent_id":"a16ef6908e56f75d6","session_id":"912108fb-652c-486d-bf9a-f0099a27506b","uuid":"bb7859aa-7fc5-4fd6-91f6-2c0db3771944","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:47:23.649Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99a6572f3772e3ff","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
