{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c2d0bbd7dfa5551","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Per-project idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a per-project idle and stale resource report view in the\n34\tRHOAI web console, giving cluster administrators visibility into resources\n35\tthat are sitting idle: workbenches nobody has touched in weeks that keep\n36\ttheir volumes and reservations, and old pipeline runs that accumulate stored\n37\tartifacts. The report surfaces, per project, an idle-workbench section\n38\t(last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from the notebook\n39\tcontroller's activity tracking, and a stale pipeline-run section (completed\n40\truns older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from\n41\tKubeflow Pipelines run metadata. Both report sections are exportable as CSV\n42\tso administrators can reclaim capacity with confidence.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Add a per-project report surface in the web console that shows idle and stale resources.\n47\t- Idle-workbench report section: per workbench, show last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking), owner, and reserved resources (volumes and reservations).\n48\t- Stale pipeline-run report section: list completed pipeline runs older than a configurable age threshold that retain artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n49\t- Make the stale-run age threshold configurable.\n50\t- CSV export of either report (idle-workbench report and stale pipeline-run report).\n51\t- Validate that the report data correctly reflects the two passive data sources: the notebook controller's last-activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run completion metadata (no code changes to those components are in scope).\n52\t- No automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and no cost/chargeback calculations (out of scope per strategy).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given a project with workbenches of varying activity, when an administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then each workbench is listed with its last activity, owner, and reserved resources, and the last-activity values match the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n57\t- Given a project with completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run report, then runs completed before the configured age threshold are listed with their retained artifacts, and the listing matches Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n58\t- Given the configurable age threshold, when an administrator changes it, then the stale pipeline-run report reflects the new threshold.\n59\t- Given either report, when an administrator triggers CSV export, then a CSV file is produced containing the report's rows and columns.\n60\t- Given the report view, when an administrator reviews it, then it contains no reclamation or deletion actions (out of scope).\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking.\n65\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n66\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled because it operates on the same report surfaces and data built for HLR-1/HLR-2.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f4c2435cd7e602d","agent_id":"a7206e9a86207a378","session_id":"912108fb-652c-486d-bf9a-f0099a27506b","uuid":"d9903c8e-2f2f-42fd-abde-ab50ba101b1b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:47.413Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c2d0bbd7dfa5551","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
